│ ## Personalized debt-management and credit-improvement strategies                                       │
│                                                                                                         │
│ ### 1. Prioritize debts by interest rate first                                                          │
│ Use the **debt avalanche** approach:                                                                    │
│ - Pay **minimums on all accounts**                                                                      │
│ - Direct all extra cash to the **highest APR debt first**                                               │
│ - Once that balance is paid off, roll that payment into the next-highest APR debt                       │
│                                                                                                         │
│ This usually minimizes total interest paid and accelerates payoff.                                      │
│                                                                                                         │
│ **Best targets first:**                                                                                 │
│ - Credit cards with the highest APR                                                                     │
│ - Store cards                                                                                           │
│ - Personal loans with elevated rates                                                                    │
│ - Any revolving debt carrying balances month to month                                                   │
│                                                                                                         │
│ ### 2. Protect your on-time payment history                                                             │
│ Your payment history is one of the most important credit factors. Even while aggressively paying down   │
│ debt:                                                                                                   │
│ - Never miss minimum payments                                                                           │
│ - Set up **autopay for at least the minimum due**                                                       │
│ - Add calendar reminders 5–7 days before due dates                                                      │
│ - Keep one month of required debt payments in checking as a buffer                                      │
│                                                                                                         │
│ Given your strong liquidity, preserving flawless payment behavior should be a top priority.             │
│                                                                                                         │
│ ### 3. Maintain low credit utilization                                                                  │
