│ - Aim for **under 30%** overall utilization                                                             │
│ - Ideally keep it **under 10%** for strongest credit-score support                                      │
│ - If one card is heavily used, pay it down even if another has a slightly higher rate, especially if    │
│ that card is near its limit                                                                             │
│                                                                                                         │
│ This helps both risk management and score improvement.                                                  │
│                                                                                                         │
│ ### 4. Keep existing credit accounts open                                                               │
│ If your current accounts are in good standing:                                                          │
│ - Avoid closing older credit cards unless they have burdensome annual fees or fraud concerns            │
│ - Older accounts help your **average age of credit**                                                    │
│ - Keeping unused cards open can also improve utilization by preserving available credit                 │
│                                                                                                         │
│ If a card has a fee, compare:                                                                           │
│ - Annual fee cost                                                                                       │
│ - Benefits received                                                                                     │
│ - Impact of closure on utilization and account age                                                      │
│                                                                                                         │
