╰─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
╭─ ← RESPONSE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ For anything involving dispute resolution, fraud detection, or account security, the normal process     │
│ should be a Human-in-the-Loop review by a qualified banking professional.                               │
│                                                                                                         │
│ Typical flow:                                                                                           │
│ 1. Intake and triage                                                                                    │
│    - The issue is reported by the customer or detected by monitoring systems.                           │
│    - Basic details are collected: account, transaction, timing, device/location context, and customer   │
│ statement.                                                                                              │
│                                                                                                         │
│ 2. Immediate risk controls                                                                              │
│    - A banking professional assesses urgency.                                                           │
│    - They may place temporary safeguards such as account monitoring, card restrictions, or              │
│ authentication challenges if needed.                                                                    │
│                                                                                                         │
│ 3. Human review                                                                                         │
│    - A trained fraud, disputes, or security specialist reviews the case.                                │
│    - They evaluate transaction patterns, account history, fraud indicators, and any supporting          │
│ evidence.                                                                                               │
│                                                                                                         │
│ 4. Customer verification                                                                                │
│    - The bank may contact the customer through verified channels.                                       │
│    - Identity verification is typically required before discussing sensitive details or taking action.  │
│                                                                                                         │
│ 5. Case classification                                                                                  │
│    - The reviewer determines whether it is:                                                             │
│      - suspected fraud,                                                                                 │
│      - a billing/merchant dispute,                                                                      │
│      - an account takeover concern,                                                                     │
│      - or another security-related issue.                                                               │
│                                                                                                         │
│ 6. Action and escalation                                                                                │
│    - Depending on findings, the specialist may:                                                         │
│      - freeze or secure access,                                                                         │
│      - block cards or transactions,                                                                     │
│      - open a dispute case,                                                                             │
│      - escalate to investigations/compliance,                                                           │
│      - or request additional documentation.                                                             │
│                                                                                                         │
│ 7. Documentation and audit trail                                                                        │
│    - All actions, decisions, and evidence are logged for compliance and review.                         │
│                                                                                                         │
│ 8. Resolution and follow-up                                                                             │
│    - The customer is informed of next steps, timelines, and any temporary or final outcomes.            │
│    - Additional monitoring may continue until the risk is cleared.                                      │
│                                                                                                         │
│ If you want, I can also help you draft a concise customer-facing policy statement for this requirement. │
